 "brief": "A hook that hangs over a 25 mm diameter closet rod and holds a 5 kg bag. PLA, FDM, printed flat\n(layers along Y), 10 mm thick (y = -5 to 5). The rod runs along Y at the origin; the hook must\nnot intrude into it (keep a 12.8 mm radius clear) and should wrap its top half: give it a\n3 mm thick saddle over the rod (the half ring from 12.8 to 15.8 mm radius, z >= 0). The bag's\nstrap hangs on a 10 mm bar along Y at (0, 0, -80), so leave that bar's 5.2 mm radius clear\nand give it a 3 mm ring of material, closed except for an opening 8 mm wide on the +X side so\nthe strap can be slipped on. Fits in x = -25 to 25, z = -92 to 20. Bags get yanked off, call it\n2x the weight. Safety factor 2.",
